  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nA chance of precipitation will follow the exiting shortwave trough \non Wednesday as a deeper closed low drops down the coast. Initially \nthe low is fairly broad as it spans the exiting trough. This will \nkeep a 30-60% chance of showers across SE Oregon and the w-central \nID mtns through Thursday. Precipitation retracts westward on Friday \nas the low consolidates along the Oregon coast and the region falls \nunder a drier southerly flow, out of the reach of the deeper \nmoisture and dynamics. From here we'll be watching for when/how the \nlow lifts eastward as this could bring another round of showers and \npossible thunderstorms. Early guidance would indicate late in the \nweekend or early next week. The S/SW flow aloft will favor gusty \nafternoon winds over elevated terrain, the stronger gusts across \nHarney, Malheur and Owyhee counties. Late afternoon/evening wind \npushes across SE Oregon could shift winds to the NW for Thur/Fri.\nThe temperature spread (10-90%tile) increases to 20 degrees for Thur-\nSun with the ensemble mean placing high temperatures near or \nslightly below normal.",
